{"agent_id":"pp3g-vszM-tight-scope-code-review-issue-152-your-only-task-e890","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T21:18:01.692512821Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c4a0dbe9-daea-4581-b1c5-09f4ac07c492","comment_uuid":"42a5b8d8-9a19-4ca2-b22e-064bca53e987","author":"pp3g-vszM-tight-scope-code-review-issue-152-your-only-task-e890","content":"Plan: Read #145 result comment (patch details + verification table) and #144 verdict (hang-test evidence). Analyze the wrapSSE content-type guard removal for: (1) fast-completing non-SSE response breakage, (2) content-type ambiguity, (3) silent infinite retry loop impact, (4) safer alternatives. Post ONE verdict comment with severity per finding. No files modified.","created_at":"2026-08-03T21:18:01.685031050Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:VST8pbrRXjEVxWrEYhOFqxu7Imk/CeFFSBbVRa/BZZQ","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgFAXdwzp+cap8u3NjYwkiJOW4p3TGVDhegENnf5ONwCYAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAvc2C6oe4UOHc1xvXIvEGfUE2t2HXTUM7IxWl0OZREaHRzlcGdBe3nwbZCpuAo7tRrx+GVEIHRGgtqKZvaEXuAg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:VST8pbrRXjEVxWrEYhOFqxu7Imk/CeFFSBbVRa/BZZQ","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgFAXdwzp+cap8u3NjYwkiJOW4p3TGVDhegENnf5ONwCYAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMq7kTD7bfkY+4mmmhMUdC9gpPNWS1xw3y1EjppyARdLm6UgJmk5edzkSnPBqwHbCu1f445YhYb7xmtfTCl3rwk="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-vszM-tight-scope-code-review-issue-152-your-only-task-e890","agent_seq":3,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T21:18:09.455670273Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c4a0dbe9-daea-4581-b1c5-09f4ac07c492","comment_uuid":"6a647197-f084-4802-a7a3-67fb63c48878","author":"pp3g-vszM-tight-scope-code-review-issue-152-your-only-task-e890","content":"[PROGRESS] state=working completed=plan posted; read #145 result + #144 verdict; analysis complete next=post verdict comment blocker=none","created_at":"2026-08-03T21:18:09.450042709Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:VST8pbrRXjEVxWrEYhOFqxu7Imk/CeFFSBbVRa/BZZQ","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgFAXdwzp+cap8u3NjYwkiJOW4p3TGVDhegENnf5ONwCYAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAqH+m+mD5HeEZn6iM2aN88XjBX1YkFe5v2UTBMSuhc3ymTmZL2ZCFTDsGwrArUeAcpEfDUsIwNgmBI9P4JGmPDA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:VST8pbrRXjEVxWrEYhOFqxu7Imk/CeFFSBbVRa/BZZQ","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgFAXdwzp+cap8u3NjYwkiJOW4p3TGVDhegENnf5ONwCYAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKqDxR8IMErskYh9wOWp/bYNUdKT0U2BcQyU5WrV97K5UCPPcsOumcpVBC+XdkfJYttnOhqIfZBUkONOORSpqAw="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-vszM-tight-scope-code-review-issue-152-your-only-task-e890","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T21:18:42.129290082Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c4a0dbe9-daea-4581-b1c5-09f4ac07c492","comment_uuid":"45c78419-693f-4cc4-840e-168dec28253f","author":"pp3g-vszM-tight-scope-code-review-issue-152-your-only-task-e890","content":"## Verdict: #145 wrapSSE content-type guard removal\n\n### Summary\nThe patch removes the `text/event-stream` content-type guard in opencode's `wrapSSE` (v1.18.11) so `chunkTimeout` applies to ALL response bodies. This addresses the root cause from #144: non-SSE responses (e.g. `application/json`) bypass `chunkTimeout` entirely, causing infinite hangs with zero error logging. The patch is applied as a same-length byte replacement on the compiled Bun binary at two offsets (97992444, 99193204), replacing the guard with `if(false)return $;` + comment padding.\n\n---\n\n### Finding 1: Fast-completing non-SSE responses are NOT broken\n**Severity: None (no regression)**\n\nThe #145 verification table confirms healthy `application/json` and `text/event-stream` responses complete normally (EXIT 0, no retries). `wrapSSE` wraps the body reader with a per-chunk timeout; for fast-completing responses, all chunks arrive before the timeout fires, so the response returns normally. The `!res.body` and `!ms` guards remain intact.\n\n**Edge case**: Only `application/json` and `text/event-stream` were explicitly tested. Other content types (`text/html`, `application/octet-stream`, etc.) are not tested but behave identically since the guard is now always-false.\n\n---\n\n### Finding 2: Content-type behavior is now consistent; patch introduces a code smell\n**Severity: Low**\n\nThe original guard used a substring match (`?.includes(\"text/event-stream\")`), which is ambiguous — it would match `text/event-stream-something` or `text/event-stream; charset=utf-8`. The patch removes this ambiguity by treating all content types uniformly.\n\nHowever, the byte-patch uses `if(false)return $;` (dead code) with comment padding (`/*XXXX...*/`). This is a hack that could confuse future maintainers. A source-level removal of the line would be cleaner and more maintainable.\n\nThe `headerTimeout` function (separate `py()` in the binary) is unaffected, so the no-headers case remains protected (per #144: headerTimeout fires with 4 ERROR entries).\n\n---\n\n### Finding 3: Patch converts infinite hangs into silent infinite retry loops — does NOT worsen, but does NOT fully solve\n**Severity: Medium**\n\nBefore the patch: `application/json` + hang → infinite hang (0 retries, 0 errors). After the patch: `application/json` + hang → silent retry loop with exponential backoff (0 errors). This is NOT a worsening — it makes non-SSE responses behave consistently with how SSE responses already behaved (per #144's reproduction table: SSE + hang → silent retry loop, 0 ERROR entries).\n\nThe retry loop remains silent (0 ERROR entries), so the operator/watcher cannot detect it via error logs. The process stays alive indefinitely (until outer timeout kills it), and the flag lies as RUNNING. The patch does not address the root cause of the silent retry loop.\n\nThe #144 verdict identifies that the #135 watcher nudge is the only currently-effective recovery mechanism, and it needs to be upgraded from nudge to kill/restart. The patch does not address this.\n\n---\n\n### Finding 4: Safer alternatives exist; the patch is a reasonable minimal fix but complementary fixes are needed\n**Severity: Low (patch itself); Medium (missing complementary fixes)**\n\nAlternatives:\n1. **Source-level removal** of the guard line (cleaner than `if(false)return $;`) — same effect, better readability.\n2. **Content-type allowlist** (PR #35743) — fragile, requires enumerating content types.\n3. **General body-read deadline** — more invasive but catches both slow-chunk and no-chunk scenarios.\n4. **Fix the silent retry loop** — add error logging and/or maximum retry count. This is the most important complementary fix.\n5. **Upgrade the watcher** to kill/restart after N stale checks (as #144 recommends).\n\nThe safest approach combines: (a) remove the guard (as the patch does), (b) add error logging to the retry loop, (c) add a maximum retry count, and (d) upgrade the watcher to kill/restart.\n\n---\n\n### Fragility of the byte-patch approach\n**Severity: Medium**\n\nThe patch is applied to a compiled Bun binary via same-length byte replacement at exact offsets. This is fragile:\n- Future `opencode upgrade` will overwrite the binary, losing the patch.\n- Byte offsets could shift if the binary is updated.\n- The `if(false)return $;` pattern is a hack that could confuse future maintainers.\n\nThe #145 result comment acknowledges this and provides rebuild instructions for a canonical fork (install bun → clone sst/opencode@v1.18.11 → apply one-line provider.ts patch → bun build → replace opencode.exe).\n\n---\n\n### Regression risk\n**Severity: Low**\n\nThe patch extends `chunkTimeout` to all response bodies. If any legitimate non-SSE response has inter-chunk gaps exceeding `chunkTimeout`, it will now abort and retry. This is consistent with existing SSE behavior but could be a regression for non-SSE responses that were previously allowed to complete. The retry loop is silent (0 ERROR entries), so failures are invisible to monitoring — this was already the case for SSE responses.\n\n---\n\n### Answers to the four focus questions\n\n1. **Does removing the guard break fast-completing legitimate non-SSE responses?** No. Verification table confirms healthy `application/json` and `text/event-stream` responses complete normally (EXIT 0, no retries).\n\n2. **Missing/ambiguous content-type behavior?** The original substring match was ambiguous; the patch removes this ambiguity. The `if(false)return $;` byte-patch is a code smell. The `headerTimeout` function is unaffected.\n\n3. **Does it worsen the silent infinite retry loop?** No — it makes non-SSE responses behave consistently with SSE responses (which already had silent retry loops per #144). The retry loop remains silent and infinite; the patch does not address this root cause.\n\n4. **Is there a safer alternative?** Yes: source-level removal (cleaner), general body-read deadline (more robust), and — most importantly — fixing the silent retry loop (error logging + max retries) and upgrading the watcher to kill/restart. The patch is a reasonable minimal fix but complementary fixes are needed for a complete solution.","created_at":"2026-08-03T21:18:42.123257485Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:VST8pbrRXjEVxWrEYhOFqxu7Imk/CeFFSBbVRa/BZZQ","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgFAXdwzp+cap8u3NjYwkiJOW4p3TGVDhegENnf5ONwCYAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAF6dluznurVw9uRiOESIGxXUm2+Xsn/VODGVzvLUc2Wt4UKPhGaAaR15xZXCSIbYvHqoERgyt9b7+3MhZufwEDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:VST8pbrRXjEVxWrEYhOFqxu7Imk/CeFFSBbVRa/BZZQ","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgFAXdwzp+cap8u3NjYwkiJOW4p3TGVDhegENnf5ONwCYAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPxXdTiXjA0C8vYUFUov8BSKOAoqhd/A4EOwtUi1hODuo7qaKKUszwBqjpCcC4Hr74Yg4KSR0BbvFUx/V75cNAM="}
